            <ArticleTitle>Unruptured left cornual pregnancy: case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1137-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Cornual pregnancy is a rare condition. The morbidity and mortality are directly related to the length of time for diagnosis. The present paper reports a case of unruptured left cornual pregnancy which was diagnosed by the patient's symptom, physical examination and positive urine pregnancy test. Ultrasonography confirmed the diagnosis. Left cornual resection was carried out in the present case without immediate or long-term complication.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
